{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Implement a transaction context object created once per transaction invocation (prioritizing thread-safety over marginal performance gains) and pass it as the first parameter to Java contract methods, mirroring the Node.js programming model. The context wraps the ChaincodeStub and related APIs; no mutable state is shared across transactions.",
    "U2/U3: Promote protos/utils to a new top-level protoutils Go package, update every internal import path in the repository, and accept this as a breaking change without maintaining a backward-compatibility shim (cleanup intent of the story).",
    "U4: Backport by cherry-picking the Kafka health-check commits from master onto the release-1.4 branch, adapting only where the 1.4 code has diverged; no redesign of the feature.",
    "U5: Choose the explicit approach: introduce a read-only chaincode invocation (query) path that channel Readers may call. Enforce read-only semantics by validating that the simulation read-write set contains no writes (rejecting any Puts), and map the access-control check for this path to the channel Readers policy instead of Writers.",
    "U6: Add a dedicated peer configuration option (e.g., CORE_PEER_DISCOVERY_EXTERNALENDPOINT) that is independent of the gossip external endpoint, used only by Service Discovery when advertising the peer; fall back to the gossip endpoint when unset to preserve current behavior.",
    "U7: Expose version information through the existing operations service framework as a new authenticated HTTP endpoint (/version) on both peer and orderer, returning JSON with version and commit SHA.",
    "U8: Refactor the Go samples to idiomatic style: gofmt/goimports/golint clean, explicit error handling, idiomatic naming and package layout, and removal of C-like patterns."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "U2 and U3 are identical duplicate user stories describing the same refactoring; the work is estimated once.",
    "All work is performed by a single developer; estimates are effort in person-days (1 workday = 8 hours), not elapsed calendar time.",
    "Estimates cover design, implementation, unit/integration testing, and documentation; maintainer code-review wait time and release-management overhead are excluded, except for the explicitly listed integration and release activities.",
    "A working development environment, build tooling, and CI pipeline for the Hyperledger Fabric repositories already exist; no environment setup effort is required.",
    "U1 targets the fabric-chaincode-java contract programming model.",
    "U4 targets the existing release-1.4 branch; the Kafka version and cluster infrastructure are unchanged.",
    "U2 involves only Go package relocation (no changes to .proto definitions or generated artifacts).",
    "U5 requires peer-side changes only; existing SDK query capability is reused and no SDK changes are needed.",
    "U8 concerns the Go samples in the fabric-samples repository; only sample code is changed, not fabric core.",
    "All eight user stories are delivered together as one software increment/release."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A-01",
      "activity_name": "U1: Design transaction context API and thread-safety model",
      "activity_description": "Define the Java Context class API, its relationship to ChaincodeStub, the per-transaction instantiation model, and how contract methods receive the context parameter.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-02",
      "activity_name": "U1: Implement per-transaction context and injection into contract methods",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Context class, per-invocation creation, and the dispatch/reflection mechanism that passes the context as the first parameter to Java contract methods.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-03",
      "activity_name": "U1: Unit and integration tests for transaction context",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for the context API and per-transaction isolation (including concurrent invocation scenarios) plus integration tests with sample Java contracts.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-04",
      "activity_name": "U1: Developer documentation and Javadoc",
      "activity_description": "Document the transaction context API, usage patterns, and thread-safety guarantees for contract developers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-05",
      "activity_name": "U2/U3: Impact analysis of protos/utils usages",
      "activity_description": "Inventory all packages and files importing protos/utils and plan the move to the new protoutils package.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-06",
      "activity_name": "U2/U3: Move protos/utils to protoutils and update references",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the package, rename import paths across the entire codebase, and adjust package documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-07",
      "activity_name": "U2/U3: Build, CI and regression verification",
      "activity_description": "Fix any build breakage, run the full build and regression suites, and verify CI pipelines pass after the package move.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-08",
      "activity_name": "U4: Analyze master Kafka health-check changes versus 1.4 codebase",
      "activity_description": "Identify the commits implementing Kafka health checks on master and assess divergence points in the release-1.4 branch.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-09",
      "activity_name": "U4: Backport Kafka health checks to release-1.4",
      "activity_description": "Cherry-pick and adapt the health-check implementation onto the 1.4 branch, resolving conflicts and API differences.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-10",
      "activity_name": "U4: Backport verification tests",
      "activity_description": "Run and adapt unit/integration tests for the health checks on 1.4, including Kafka cluster failure scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-11",
      "activity_name": "U5: Design read-only chaincode invocation and ACL model",
      "activity_description": "Design the read-only invoke/query path, the read-write set validation that rejects writes, and the mapping of the ACL check to the channel Readers policy.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-12",
      "activity_name": "U5: Implement read-only invocation path and ACL enforcement",
      "activity_description": "Implement the peer-side changes: read-only proposal handling, simulation write-set validation, and ACL changes allowing channel Readers to execute queries.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-13",
      "activity_name": "U5: Unit tests",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests covering ACL decisions for Readers vs Writers and rejection of write operations on the read-only path.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-14",
      "activity_name": "U5: Integration and end-to-end tests",
      "activity_description": "End-to-end tests with identities holding only Reader permission invoking query chaincode, including negative tests for writes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-15",
      "activity_name": "U5: Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Update access-control and chaincode invocation documentation describing Reader-based query capability.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-16",
      "activity_name": "U6: Design discovery external endpoint configuration",
      "activity_description": "Define the new peer configuration option, its interaction/fallback with the gossip external endpoint, and the service discovery response changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-17",
      "activity_name": "U6: Implement configuration option and service discovery changes",
      "activity_description": "Implement config parsing, plumb the endpoint into the discovery service so SDK clients receive the advertised external endpoint.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-18",
      "activity_name": "U6: Unit and integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Tests for configuration handling, fallback behavior, and discovery responses returning the configured endpoint (including a docker-network scenario).",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-19",
      "activity_name": "U6: Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the new configuration option and its use for service discovery without DNS.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-20",
      "activity_name": "U7: Design operations-service version endpoint",
      "activity_description": "Specify the /version endpoint response format (version, commit SHA) and authentication, consistent for peer and orderer.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-21",
      "activity_name": "U7: Implement version information in peer and orderer operations service",
      "activity_description": "Add the version handler to the operations server of both peer and orderer, sourcing build-time version metadata.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-22",
      "activity_name": "U7: Tests",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests for the version endpoint on both node types, including authentication checks.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-23",
      "activity_name": "U7: Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the new operations endpoint for operators, including an example response.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-24",
      "activity_name": "U8: Review samples and define idiomatic Go conventions",
      "activity_description": "Audit the existing Go samples, identify non-idiomatic patterns, and agree the target conventions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-25",
      "activity_name": "U8: Refactor Go samples to idiomatic style",
      "activity_description": "Rewrite the samples applying the conventions (error handling, naming, structure, lint cleanliness).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-26",
      "activity_name": "U8: Verify and test refactored samples",
      "activity_description": "Build, lint, and execute the refactored samples against a test network to confirm unchanged behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-27",
      "activity_name": "Release: Cross-story integration and full regression",
      "activity_description": "Integrate all story branches, resolve cross-story conflicts, and run the full regression and CI suites for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-28",
      "activity_name": "Release: Release notes and consolidated documentation",
      "activity_description": "Prepare release notes covering all stories (including the U2/U3 breaking change notice) and consolidate documentation updates.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 76
  }
}

